@host = http://localhost:3001

### 1. Public route: only the global logger runs
GET {{host}}/ HTTP/1.1

### 2. Private route without API key: requireApiKey returns 401
GET {{host}}/private HTTP/1.1

### 3. Private route with a wrong API key: requireApiKey returns 401
GET {{host}}/private HTTP/1.1
x-api-key: wrong

### 4. Private route with a valid API key: 200
GET {{host}}/private HTTP/1.1
x-api-key: secret

### 5. POST /lists without API key: stops at requireApiKey (401)
POST {{host}}/lists HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Groceries"
}

### 6. POST /lists with API key: requireApiKey, then measureResponseTime logs the duration (201)
POST {{host}}/lists HTTP/1.1
x-api-key: secret
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Groceries"
}

### 7. PUT /lists/:id without API key: 401
PUT {{host}}/lists/1 HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Office Supplies"
}

### 8. PUT /lists/:id with API key: 200
PUT {{host}}/lists/1 HTTP/1.1
x-api-key: secret
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Office Supplies"
}

### 9. DELETE under /admin without API key: app.use('/admin', requireApiKey) returns 401
DELETE {{host}}/admin/lists/1 HTTP/1.1

### 10. DELETE under /admin with API key: 200
DELETE {{host}}/admin/lists/1 HTTP/1.1
x-api-key: secret
